{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>YHWH your Elohim has multiplied you.</b> In Egypt — for you went down there seventy souls and came up six hundred thousand footmen, and today you are beyond number. Or one may say הרבה אתכם means 'made you great,' from the expression (Jeremiah 39) רבי המלך, which is interpreted as 'the great ones of the king.'" "<b>And today you are like the stars of the heavens.</b> He likened them to the stars in respect to multitude, and this is what it said: לרוב." "<b>And by way of the Midrash</b> in Eileh HaDevarim Rabbah: ״והנכם היום ככוכבי השמים, וחניתכם היום ככוכבי השמים״ — just as the Holy One, blessed be He, showed Abraham, for He showed him all the constellations surrounding the Shekhinah, so the banner of the camp of Israel, three to every direction, with His glory in the middle — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: just as the constellations surround Me and My glory is in the middle, so your children are destined to multiply and encamp banner by banner, and My Shekhinah in the middle, as it is said (Numbers 2:16–17): ״ונסע אהל מועד״ וגו'. Hence you may say: ״והנכם היום ככוכבי השמים, וחניתכם היום ככוכבי השמים״ — end quote."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The citation '(ירמיה לט)' in comment 0 points to Jeremiah 39:13, where רבי המלך appears; the printed chapter number appears to follow the Hebrew verse-counting tradition and has been left as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:45.233495383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}